Oh! There we go!

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:37.400
*loud noise* OH! That's the bad man...

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.400
*Scott grunting* (Mark's face)

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:52.000
*Intermittent grunting*

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.000
*mumbling, indistinct*

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:56.300
Back.. *coughs*

00:12:56.350 --> 00:13:02.800
Where... Where are you?! *radio* You really love your family.. *static*

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:04.399
...Don't you?

00:13:04.399 --> 00:13:09.900
*panting, grunting*

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:12.040
*radio, indistinct* Y'know?

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:16.500
Michael: Survive the night.. just wait for 6:00 a.m. and it will all be over..

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:19.400
That's how it worked there before... Right?

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:21.900
Michael, indistinct: We survived their games...

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:28.400
*Scott groaning*

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:31.800
*shaky breathing*

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:36.800
Michael: This night... won't go away until you've been consumed by the fire.

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:44.200
Scott: What of them... If I have to go...?

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:48.600
Will you please promise me... They'll be safe...?

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:52.600
*radio static*

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:57.600
Scott, weakly: Promise me... You won't hurt them...

00:13:58.300 --> 00:13:59.600
Please!

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:05.600
*Scott sobbing*

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:07.600
*Scott gasps*

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:12.600
*Scott groaning, animatronics laughing(?)* *(Random insert)look into my eyes*

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:14.720
Okay! That's weird..

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:21.160
*Scott screaming in pain* (probably ultimate climax)

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:27.300
Hmm, I don't know about that...

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:32.200
Something fishy going on here...

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:34.200
Young Nick: Mommy! Daddy's coming out of the house!

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.000
Val: Honey?!

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:37.700
Scott: Val! I'm here!

00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:39.700
Young Nick: Daddy!

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:44.000
Val, sobbing: Oh, hon, I was SO worried...

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:47.000
Scott: It's okay, Val. It's okay... We're safe now.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:49.000
Scott: Have you called 911?

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:52.200
Val: Yes... Yes, I did. As soon as we got out, I called them.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.800
Val: Like, a-a few hours ago...

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:57.300
Val: They said they'll be here as soon as they could...

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:00.900
Val: Oh my god... You stayed inside there for so long!

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:05.000
Val: I thought you--
Scott, monotone: But I didn't. Don't worry. Everybody is fine.

00:15:05.839 --> 00:15:09.200
Nick: Daddy, what happened to home? Why is it burning?!

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.200
Nick: Is Michael still in there?

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:15.110
Scott: You're safe. *mumbling* all that matters.

00:15:15.110 --> 00:15:17.000
Scott: You're safe.

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:21.200
Nick, worried: Dad?
Val: Everything... Everything is gone!

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:25.100
Scott, robotically: You are safe. That's all that matters.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.400
Nick: Dad! You're acting weird...

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:32.000
Scott: You are safe now. That's all that matters.

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:36.500
Val, scared: Honey, are you all--
Scott: You are safe... That's all that matters.

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:49.600
*Scott keeps repeating himself* Nick, scared: Daddy, no!
Val, crying: Oh, my god.. Oh my god!

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:54.860
*Scott's voice starts glitching*

00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:58.980
Animatronic in Scott's voice: See, they're safe now.

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:01.500
Just as you wanted...

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:04.900
Thank you for your cooperation, Scott Cawthon.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:07.000
I'll take care of everything from here...

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:08.900
*Mark scoffs*

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.000
Well, alright then!

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:16.000
That's just how that-- *stuttering* That's the way that that goes

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:17.000
*more stuttering*

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:19.300
That is the thing that is that. (What?)

00:16:19.399 --> 00:16:20.750
Well!

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:24.300
So, that's that then. Uh...

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:26.400
*sighs in disbelief*

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:28.510
Uh, okay, anyway, so

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:31.330
Body was taken over by Michael...

00:16:32.089 --> 00:16:37.000
And now Scott's... dead? Got the purple guy treatment to him or something like that?

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:41.000
I have no idea, but either way this was... Amazing.

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:44.049
AMAZING! I'm not even lying about that, this was amazing

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:48.800
This is, by far, THE best Five Nights at Freddy's fan game ever made and

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:53.469
I don't know! I-I kind of want to say, I enjoyed this

00:16:54.230 --> 00:16:56.900
Even more than the actual games themselves!

00:16:56.900 --> 00:16:58.900
Like, just from a gameplay stand point

00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:01.700
And-and I'm only speaking from a gameplay stand point because

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:03.550
Obviously, this game would not exist

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:06.300
if those games, uh, didn't exist before

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:11.700
and obviously inspired this. I'm not saying one is better than the other but just from like an enjoyability

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:14.140
Factor like there's a lot of mystery here

00:17:14.140 --> 00:17:16.000
There's a lot of story. Each level

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:17.800
had a unique mechanic!

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.800
An entirely unique mechanic!

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:23.300
Each of those levels could have been their own self-contained games

00:17:23.329 --> 00:17:25.160
with ramping difficulty!

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:29.000
But instead they were all one, and it was just awesome!

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:32.400
The experience was great! The developer of this game

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:35.000
is just-- they made-- they made something GREAT!

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:37.000
They made something literally great

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:39.609
And it was free! And I would have paid money for this,

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:43.800
I would have paid 20 bucks for this! I would have gladly paid 20 bucks for this!

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:46.000
Oh, man!

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:49.900
I don't know how Scott feels about, uh, him being murdered in a fan game, but yeah

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:51.900
It's whatever, there's probably more...

